= Rapallo

On 16 April, in a hotel at Rapallo, Walther Rathenau and Georgy Chicherin sign a treaty. Germany and Soviet Russia give up all claims on each other and restore relations. The Allies at Genoa are furious.

The treaty does not mention General von Seeckt's officers, who have been travelling to Russia for a year, or the Junkers works that is to build aircraft near Moscow where no Allied inspector will see it. Several people in the Zentrale know about both.

- @hail: Hail the treaty, and say nothing about the generals.
- @warn: Welcome it, and ask in the Reichstag what the Reichswehr is doing in Russia.

@hail
subtitle: Trotsky and Radek are pleased.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('trotsky', 6);
RG.ecci('radek', 4);
Q.e22_rapallo = 1;
Q.independence -= 4;
!}

*Die Rote Fahne* prints the treaty under the headline "The Blockade Is Broken".

@warn
subtitle: The Reichswehr loses a secret, and Trotsky loses patience with us.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('trotsky', -8);
RG.ecci('radek', -5);
Q.e22_rapallo = 2;
Q.independence += 7;
Q.army_loyalty -= 3;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
!}

Our deputy asks the Reichswehr minister about German officers in Russia. The minister denies everything. Radek's next letter to the Zentrale is not shown to the typists.
